      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This section reports an exploratory principal axis factor analysis (quartimax rotation) of the Dutch BAS-2 items, demonstrating a one-dimensional factor structure with one eigenvalue > 1 explaining 53.24% of variance. It notes strong sampling adequacy (KMO = .93), significant Bartlett's test (p < .001), high item loadings (> .61) except Item 5 (.33) which was retained for multiple reasons. The section does not label any study number (e.g., 'Study 1') nor provide participant/sample demographics or BMI-related correlations.",
